        <item>
        <title>Upcoming Show in January</title>
        <link>http://localhost:1313/thesneers/p/upcoming-show-in-january/</link>
        <pubDate>Thu, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <author>info@thesneers.com (The Sneers)</author>
        <guid>http://localhost:1313/thesneers/p/upcoming-show-in-january/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="http://localhost:1313/thesneers/p/upcoming-show-in-january/7948.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Upcoming Show in January" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Join The Sneers on Jan. 10 at the legendary Milkie’s on Elmwood Ave. in Buffalo as they take the stage for a bill that includes Buffalo’s Broken Locker and Racehearse, and Good Squad from Binghamton! Doors at 8:30 pm. $10 admission, 21+.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
        </item>
        <item>
        <title>Songs in the Key of Mike</title>
        <link>http://localhost:1313/thesneers/p/songs-in-the-key-of-mike/</link>
        <pubDate>Tue, 21 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <author>info@thesneers.com (The Sneers)</author>
        <guid>http://localhost:1313/thesneers/p/songs-in-the-key-of-mike/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="http://localhost:1313/2.jpeg" alt="Featured image of post Songs in the Key of Mike" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our new EP is out! “Songs in the Key of Mike” is available on all streams, including Bandcamp and Spotify. Produced by John Angelo. Artwork by Andrew Burgess. Dedicated to our man, Michael McMahon Jr., who after the recording of this record moved on to pursue new adventures. Mike had been with us since the band’s inception. He’s an awesome human and we wish him the best in all endeavors. This EP rips! Please check it out! Track list includes: ‘Fuck These Fucking Nazis,’ ‘Katy Perry,’ ‘Tool Bag,’ and ‘Whip’ (revisited). Soon to be released in physical format too from 1120 Records. Stay tuned!&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
        </item>
